wait wat do you mean storage server!!
i mean all the machine are capable of being storage server , 
here's what you need to understand each system can serve as a storage server begining from ai1, when the user in the app creates a filestore it will start filling up the nodes begining from ai1 sequentially once that is full it will move on to the next and so on .
and depending on the running instances and the configuration on each node the backend will decided where the compute (docker instance) should be started in , if on the same node as the storage then the connect or mount is local else it will be nvme-of connect to the storage whereever it resides

for eaxmple this is how we start the ai5 machine
PROVISION_SECRET=e75064ca1702889e4f519d4ad40dfbd5f18dbdb67db7f365 ENABLE_NFS_AUTOMOUNT=true STORAGE_IP=10.10.100.138 FLASK_HOST=0.0.0.0 FLASK_PORT=9999 NFS_EXPORT_CLIENT="10.10.100.130(rw,sync,no_subtree_check,no_root_squash) 10.10.100.132(rw,sync,no_subtree_check,no_root_squash) 10.10.100.134(rw,sync,no_subtree_check,no_root_squash) 10.10.100.136(rw,sync,no_subtree_check,no_root_squash) 127.0.0.1" python3 app.py



